  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the executive law, in relation to expanding eligibility for\nvictims and survivors of crime to access victim compensation funds; and to\namend a chapter of the laws of 2023 amending the executive law relating to\nexpanding eligibility for victims and survivors of crime to access victim\ncompensation funds by removing the mandatory law enforcement reporting\nrequirement, providing alternative forms of evidence that would show that a\nqualifying crime was committed and the confidentiality of certain records, as\nproposed in legislative bills numbers S. 214-A and A. 2105-A, in relation to\nthe effectiveness thereof",
    "basePrintNo": "S8071",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S8071-2023",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [
      {
       "alternate": false,
       "chamber": "SENATE",
       "districtCode": 31,
       "fullName": "Robert Jackson",
       "imgName": "1050_Robert_Jackson.jpg",
       "incumbent": true,
       "memberId": 1230,
       "sessionMemberId": 2017,
       "sessionYear": 2023,
       "shortName": "JACKSON"
      }
     ],
     "size": 1
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §§631, 625 & 633, Exec L; amd §7, Chap of 2023 (as proposed in S.214-A & A.2105-A)",
    "lawSection": "Executive Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S8071\n\nSPONSOR: MYRIE\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the executive law, in relation to expanding eligibility\nfor victims and survivors of crime to access victim compensation funds;\nand to amend a chapter of the laws of 2023 amending the executive law\nrelating to expanding eligibility for victims and survivors of crime to\naccess victim compensation funds by removing the mandatory law enforce-\nment reporting requirement, providing alternative forms of evidence that\nwould show that a qualifying crime was committed and the confidentiality\nof certain records, as proposed in legislative bills numbers S. 214-A\nand A. 2105-A, in relation to the effectiveness thereof\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis is a chapter amendment that makes changes to the executive law.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nThis amendment creates a new definition for \"support agency for survi-\nvors of crime\", creates a new definition for \"victim services provider\"\nwhich includes physicians and local victims services providers, amends\nthe definition of \"criminal justice agency\", allows for alternative\nforms of evidence if accompanied by an attestation, and extends the\neffective date to December 31, 2025.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis legislation is a negotiated change to the underlying chapter. The\nExecutive aimed to clarify the types of alternative evidence that would\nbe accepted if the individual did not report the crime to a criminal\njustice agency.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nChapter amendment to Chapter 695 of the Laws of 2023.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect December 31, 2025 and further shall apply to\nall claims filed on or after such effective date.\n",
